<title>ZIMBABWE: NTS raises interim shr, div steady.</title>
<headline>NTS raises interim shr, div steady.</headline>
<dateline>HARARE 1997-03-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Half-year ended December 25.</p>
<p>		  (all figures in Z$ million unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr (cts)		   39.4	vs   38.4</p>
<p>    Div (cts)		    9.5	vs   9.5</p>
<p>    After-tax profit	   8.90     vs   8.65</p>
<p>    Pre-tax		     13.99     vs   13.56</p>
<p>    Tax			    5.10     vs   4.91</p>
<p>    Interest paid		2.15     vs   1.08</p>
<p>    Turnover		   144.52     vs   118.67</p>
<p>Div payable April 15</p>
<p>on register March 21</p>
<p>Full name: National Tyre Services Ltd</p>
<p>Note -- The company anticipated that growth in turnover would continue into the second half of the financial year. It said forecasts of firm economic growth in Zimbabwe in 1997 would impact positively on the results for the second half of the financial year and even into the 1997/98 period.</p>
<p>-- Harare newsroom +263-4 72 52 28/9</p>
</text>
